<h1>Keola Jean-Joseph</h1>
<p>24th Police District Council, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027. Incumbent.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Filed nominating petitions on Oct. 19, 2026 for reelection. Their council biography says Keo seeks to make sure every resident&#39;s voice is heard on the council.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>24th District Council member and its community engagement coordinator; works at the Lighthouse Institute supporting people in recovery through research; six years of community organizing on mutual aid and voter access; has lived in the 24th District for ten years. Uses they/them pronouns.</p>
